      ['What is a volcanic rock such as basalt?', 'a rock formed when lava cools', [['a rock made of shells', 'That is limestone. 🐚'], ['a man-made rock', 'That is concrete. 🏗️'], ['a rock of ice', 'No. 🧊']], 'Basalt forms the ocean floor and many volcanoes.'],
      ['Why does the Moon seem to change shape during the month?', 'we see a bigger or smaller part of its side lit by the Sun', [['the Earth’s shadow hides it every evening', 'That is an eclipse, which is much rarer. 🌑'], ['it shrinks and grows again', 'Its size does not change. 🌕'], ['clouds cut it up', 'No. ☁️']], 'New Moon, first quarter, full Moon, last quarter: these are the phases.'],
      ['Why can the Earth support life?', 'it has liquid water, an atmosphere and a suitable temperature', [['it is the biggest planet', 'That is Jupiter. 🪐'], ['it is the closest to the Sun', 'That is Mercury. ☀️'], ['it has rings', 'That is Saturn. 🪐']], 'The Earth is at the right distance from the Sun for water to stay liquid.']
